"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/s1547/BILLS-119s1547is.htm"}]},"sponsor":{"chamber":"Senate","district":null,"id":"D000618","name":"Sen. Daines, Steve","party":"R","state":"MT"},"stage":"on_calendar","stage_label":"On a chamber calendar","summary":"S. 1547, titled the America the Beautiful Act, amends title 54 of the United States Code to reauthorize and modify the National Parks and Public Land Legacy Restoration Fund through fiscal year 2031. The bill establishes definitions and spending limitations for deferred maintenance projects across federal land agencies, creates an entrance fee surcharge for non-resident visitors to National Park System units, and authorizes the Department of the Interior to license its intellectual property and retain associated fees.","summary_detail":{"affected_groups":[{"effect":"Subject to a newly established entrance fee surcharge in addition to standard entrance fees.","group":"Non-resident visitors to National Park System units"},{"effect":"Must adhere to new prioritization criteria, reporting requirements, maintenance definitions, and spending restrictions for deferred maintenance funds.","group":"Federal land agencies (National Park Service, Fish and Wildlife Service, Forest Service, Bureau of Land Management)"},{"effect":"Allowed to enter into licensing agreements and pay fees to cover processing and administrative costs.","group":"Qualifying entities seeking to license Department of the Interior intellectual property"}],"key_provisions":["Reauthorizes deposits into the National Parks and Public Land Legacy Restoration Fund for fiscal years 2027 through 2031 from federal onshore land revenues.","Sets minimum allocation percentages for deferred maintenance nontransportation projects within specific agencies, such as the Fish and Wildlife Service, Forest Service, and Bureau of Land Management.","Prohibits the use of Fund moneys for acquiring land, supplementing recurring operational maintenance, employee bonuses, or decommissioning certain roads.","Requires the President to submit an annual list of prioritized projects and project data sheets to Congress alongside the federal budget.","Establishes an entrance fee surcharge for non-resident visitors to National Park System units, with proceeds directed to the Restoration Fund.","Grants the Secretary of the Interior authority to license Department intellectual property to qualifying entities and expend the resulting fees."],"missing_information":["The exact dollar amounts for the non-resident visitor surcharges are not specified in the text.","The specific total annual deposit cap amount for the Restoration Fund is not explicitly stated in the provided text."],"plain_summary":"S. 1547, titled the America the Beautiful Act, amends title 54 of the United States Code to reauthorize and modify the National Parks and Public Land Legacy Restoration Fund through fiscal year 2031. The bill establishes definitions and spending limitations for deferred maintenance projects across federal land agencies, creates an entrance fee surcharge for non-resident visitors to National Park System units, and authorizes the Department of the Interior to license its intellectual property and retain associated fees.","significance":"The bill extends and alters the funding structure and project prioritization rules for addressing deferred maintenance backlogs across federal public lands and national parks, while introducing new revenue streams through visitor surcharges and intellectual property licensing."},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-25T12:02:31+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/s1547/BILLS-119s1547rs.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"America the Beautiful Act","viability":69.0,"viability_detail":{"breakdown":[{"available":true,"effective_weight":35.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Detected stage","value":"On a chamber calendar"}],"key":"stage","label":"Legislative stage","note":"S